Tame the cat.  Walk away from the mumak -- it's slower than you are.
Write E in the dust if you need to.  If you have a mirror, you can
also apply it in a pinch to scare the mumak.  Let your now tame cat
take care of the rest of the critters on the level.


There are two basic tactics for killing mumakil.  One is the "mumak
dance".  Mumakil, having speed 9, only get a move on three out of
every four turns; if you hit them on the fourth turn, they can't
counterattack.  Once you've figured out which turns are the safe ones,
you can (assuming you're at normal speed) settle into a comfortable
step-step-step-hit rhythm.  Just watch out for dead ends.

If you're fast or very fast, you'll also occasionally get free moves.
To make the most of this, turn on the "time" option and watch the turn
counter.  Whenever you make a move but the turn counter doesn't
advance, you know you'll have another move this turn which you can
safely use to hit the mumak.

This is best practiced in wiz/explore mode.  Just wish up a cursed
figurine of a mumak and play with it until you get the hang of it.

The other method of dealing with mumakil is just to keep a safe
distance and throw or zap things at it until it dies.  This is safer
and requires less attention.  The dance does, however, have the
advantage that you'll be next to the mumak when it dies, giving you a
better shot at reaching the tasty and nutritious corpse before your
pet does.

